# dns.schema — who may set each key of the `dns` subsystem (see w-conf.md).
# Format: <KEY>\t<scope>   scope: system | user | both
#
# One resolver serves the whole machine (systemd-resolved), and DoT strictness is
# a security policy — root domain.
PROVIDER	system
DOT	system
# The provider catalog is data the admin extends, so it is declared as a GLOB row
# rather than key by key — otherwise every new entry would ship undeclared, i.e.
# unconstrained, and a user file could redefine the addresses behind the admin's
# chosen provider name.
DNS_*	system
